		<entry>
		<author><name><![CDATA[Dirk Gregorius]]></name></author>
		<updated>2014-07-16T21:55:27+00:00</updated>

		<published>2014-07-16T21:55:27+00:00</published>
		<id>https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=33688#p33688</id>
		<link href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=33688#p33688"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Strategies for dealing with non-incremental broadphase]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=33688#p33688"><![CDATA[
I update the proxy in the broadphase immediately to avoid the problems you described, but I don't compute contacts directly. <br><br>For hitboxes I don't add them into the physics broadphase at all. Especially on a server/client structure you don't want to rewind those. And even in general it makes sense to avoid the hitbox traffic on the broadphase in this case. Hitboxes can be implemented very efficiently using brute force methods utilizing SIMD. I am now even leaning forwards to take triggers out the physics broadphase and have them in a separate system.<br><br>Cheers,<br>-Dirk<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Wed Jul 16, 2014 9:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
